            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "By default, Docker Buildx uses mode=min, which only caches intermediate layers for the final resulting stage of multi-stage Dockerfiles. Setting mode=max instructs BuildKit to cache intermediate layers for all stages, including builder, testing, and dependency compilation targets, dramatically improving cache hits across rebuilds."
          }
