        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono">01.</span> Build Performance &amp; Wall-Clock Benchmarks
        </h2>
        <p>
          In modern microservice architectures, un-cached container compilation is the single largest bottleneck in continuous integration pipelines. A standard Next.js or Go application with dependency installs, Prisma client compilation, and multi-stage intermediate targets easily consumes 8 to 12 minutes on GitHub-hosted runners (<code class="text-slate-200 font-mono">ubuntu-latest</code>).
        </p>
        <p>
          The table below demonstrates empirical results measured across 50 consecutive workflow runs comparing un-cached builds against various BuildKit cache strategies:
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/80 my-6">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300">
